      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={6}^{x}+5{e}^{x}$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x}+5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={6}^{x}\\ln 6+5{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={({6}^{x}\\ln 6+5{e}^{x})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & ={6}^{0}\\ln 6+5{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\ln 6+5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\ln 6+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
